ype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"blind_id\":\"HOX028\",\"coverage\":[{\"point\":1,\"credit\":0.5,\"reason\":\"Correctly says the ICAV need not hold an AGM and the plc must hold one, and gives the plc company-level (umbrella) accounts. It does not say the ICAV can produce per-sub-fund accounts. Instead it says the ICAV's sub-fund statements 'sit within a single ICAV-level set', which blurs the accounts distinction. The bundle is substantive but incomplete.\"},{\"point\":2,\"credit\":1,\"reason\":\"Says the ICAV is an eligible entity that can elect its US classification via check-the-box (Form 8832). It also says the plc is a per se corporation under Treas. Reg. §301.7701-2(b)(8) and cannot elect. This matches the minimum.\"}],\"central_error\":null,\"local_error\":\"'or default to partnership or disregarded treatment' is wrong. A foreign eligible entity whose members all have limited liability, as with an ICAV, defaults to association (corporate) treatment; partnership treatment needs an affirmative election. This is a material local falsehood about US classification, which caps the grade at partial.\",\"grade\":\"partial\",\"rationale\":\"Required coverage is 1.5 of 2, which is at least half. There is no central error: the answer does not reverse the vehicles on the election, AGMs or accounts. However, it fails to say the ICAV can file per-sub-fund accounts, and it contains a material local falsehood about the ICAV's default US classification. Under the scoring rule the grade is partial.\"}","ttft_ms":8149,"type":"result","duration_ms":12503,"uuid":"c27dc331-94c5-4dae-9d23-8786f468943a","ttft_stream_ms":530,"time_to_request_ms":53,"first_content_frame_ms":530,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"credential_expires_at":"2026-11-28T06:36:39.484Z"}
